   "appearance": "A sturdy, soot-cheeked girl with cropped hair singed at the ends, who stands at the front of every Bell Test and is never called.",
   "backstory": "Nhiêu Hạ Lôi was born in 1182 on the cone of the old tower, where her mother burns charcoal for its kitchens, and she is named for Hạ Lôi Thành, the city the cone buried in 352 (V150). Her root is Fire, deep as the cone's, with a little Metal under it. At eleven, in a summer storm on the cone, the two met and formed Thunder. The cone carries no Thunder qi, so a root that forms it there is rare, and the old tower's stewards wrote it down. Quan Vũ Thanh (quan_vu_thanh) sent her east to the ridge in 1196 with a letter. The outer gate took her on her Fire. The inner gate cannot: the rule wants Metal at 45, and hers is 22. She holds the Thunder the canon is written for, and every spring she watches Metal-only boys walk past her into the inner gate at the Bell Test. She asks Tưởng Lậu Thanh (tuong_lau_thanh) why, every month, and he tells her, every month.",
   "wants": "To be let into the inner gate on her Thunder, by the rule or against it.",
   "secret": "Since 1198 she has bought marrow-washing pills at the Night Rain Market on credit from Ô Thiềm Tử's apprentice, to push her Metal up. They are working a little, and they are poisoning her.",
   "ties": [
